# Line ending normalization
#
# Goal: enforce LF line endings on all source files for cross-platform
# consistency (gofmt 1.25+, git diff readability, blame hygiene).
#
# History: the JySecAI scanner-runtime-v2 integration commit chain
# (985010af, 630eb81e, 3d9c7c41, e38fdac0) introduced mixed line endings
# after VPS4 gofmt -w forced LF on touched files while the surrounding
# files remained CRLF. This .gitattributes file formalizes the policy:
# Go and shell sources are LF; markdown/YAML/JSON are LF; nothing is CRLF
# by default. Windows checkouts that previously worked with CRLF will
# normalize on next `git add --renormalize` or fresh clone.

# Default: detect text vs binary, normalize to LF on input, LF on output
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go source must always be LF (gofmt enforces LF output)
*.go text eol=lf

# CGo / C sources follow Go convention
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf

# Build / script sources
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.zsh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.vue text eol=lf
*.svelte text eol=lf
*.proto text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# Makefile conventionally uses LF
Makefile text eol=lf
GNUmakefile text eol=lf
*.mk text eol=lf

# Dockerfile / container
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# Git-internal text files
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitmodules text eol=lf

# Binary files (force LF handling off to avoid corruption)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.bz2 binary
*.xz binary
*.7z binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
